# Lastro

This project runs Lastro missions through the `lastro` MCP server.

The Lastro launcher delivers the verified skill bundle in your developer instructions. Its source
files are:

- `skills/lastro/explore.md`: run workflow, tools and untrusted content rules
- `skills/lastro/qa-heuristics.md`: heuristics and how to record each check
- `skills/lastro/reproduce.md`: replay protocol for findings

Start every run with `mission_context`, then `submit_mission_plan`. Show the returned plan
and charter before the first exploration action.

When the mission is a reproduction brief, follow `skills/lastro/reproduce.md`: replay the steps,
report once with `report_reproduction_result` and end the run without submitting findings.

Operate the target only with the Lastro tools. Human gates are decided with `lastro approve` in
another terminal; keep polling `approval_status` and never treat a Codex prompt as an approval.
Lastro policies, approvals and locks always win over these instructions.
